# Load the ModSecurity connector (spec §11.9).
#
# `load_module` is a main-context directive, so this file only works when
# nginx.conf includes its directory *above* the `events` block. The panel
# checks that before writing here and refuses the whole feature otherwise — it
# will not add the include to nginx.conf itself, because nginx.conf belongs to
# the nginx package (spec §10.4 rule 1).
#
# If the module was built against a different nginx, this line is where that
# shows up: `nginx -t` answers "module ... is not binary compatible", the
# config engine restores the previous state and the change never reaches a
# reload.
load_module {{ module_path }};
